      "title": "🎯 Rollout Decision — Does VAD EOU improve turn latency?",
      "type": "row"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "$datasource"
      },
      "description": "How shadow mode works: on sampled VAD-less continuous-ASR calls, the Silero fork runs observe-only. When Silero fires speech_stopped, the timestamp is recorded but nothing happens in the real path — the turn stays open and closes normally via vendor final transcript or asrTimeout. delta_ms = t_silero_speech_stopped − t_real_legacy_close. Negative = Silero detected end-of-speech that many ms before the real close (snappier). Positive = real close came first (Silero lagging or missed). Important: the advance shown is the theoretical maximum. With VAD EOU enabled, production savings are capped at asrTimeout (typically 800–2000 ms) because the code waits at most asrTimeout ms for the vendor to catch up after Silero fires. Deltas larger than asrTimeout occur when interim transcripts keep resetting the timer, but the production path would still commit at the asrTimeout boundary. Mass concentrated left of 0 ms = strong case for enabling VAD EOU. Cell values show turn counts per 5-minute window (window fixed regardless of the time-picker range — heatmap constraint). Y-axis labels use Grafana ms auto-format: values ≥ 1 s display as seconds (e.g. -2 s), smaller values stay in ms.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "hideFrom": {
              "tooltip": false,
              "viz": false,
              "legend": false
            },
            "scaleDistribution": {
              "type": "linear"
            }
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 18,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 1
      },
      "id": 2,
      "options": {
        "calculate": false,
        "cellGap": 2,
        "cellValues": {},
        "color": {
          "exponent": 0.5,
          "fill": "dark-orange",
          "mode": "scheme",
          "reverse": false,
          "scale": "exponential",
          "scheme": "Spectral",
          "steps": 128
        },
        "exemplars": {
          "color": "rgba(255,0,255,0.7)"
        },
        "filterValues": {
          "le": 1e-09
        },
        "legend": {
          "show": true
        },
        "rowsFrame": {
          "layout": "auto"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "show": true,
          "yHistogram": false
        },
        "yAxis": {
          "axisPlacement": "left",
          "reverse": false,
          "unit": "ms"
        }
      },
      "pluginVersion": "10.0.0",
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "$datasource"
          },
          "expr": "sum(increase(vg_vad_eou_shadow_delta_ms_bucket{cluster=\"$cluster\"}[5m])) by (le)",
          "format": "heatmap",
          "legendFormat": "{{le}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Delta Distribution (Silero EOS − Legacy close, ms)",
      "type": "heatmap"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "$datasource"
      },
      "description": "Share of continuous-ASR turns where Silero emitted speech_stopped (both / (both + real_only)) over the selected range. Green ≥ 90%. A high rate means Silero reliably sees end-of-speech; real_only turns are where VAD EOU would not improve latency.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "mappings": [],
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 0.8
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 0.9
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "decimals": 1
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 2,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 18,
        "y": 1
      },
      "id": 3,
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "orientation": "auto",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
