      "description": "Median VAD EOU advance: −p50(delta_ms). Positive = Silero end-of-speech was that many ms earlier than the legacy turn-close. Negative = legacy closed first. Note: actual production savings are capped at the call's asrTimeout — a p50 advance larger than asrTimeout means the turn would close at the asrTimeout boundary, not the full advance.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "mappings": [],
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
